## REFUSE AT ONCE (last line `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY`, one question; each count with a control that fires; items 1 and 2 before `.tools/b1703` is created, items 3 to 8 before the first write)
1. `/usr/bin/grep -c -E '_{4}'` of your Step-0 copy prints 0 on the STAMPED copy (the unstamped copy reads 11 such lines: the slot lines and the last line; control: a planted line adds 1); the last line begins `READ-WHOLE-BY-TUESDAY: DONE`; the JIRA, MOVE, CREATE-P, CREATE-A, RECORDS and REC-MERGE slots each read one of the words their line offers; **the BASE slot states root main, code main, the CI of code main and that no `Datasec/MPS-R` pane runs.** A slot left at its default: JIRA -> HOLD, MOVE -> NONE, CREATE-P -> NONE, CREATE-A -> NONE, RECORDS -> HOLD, REC-MERGE -> HOLD.
2. `tmux display -p -t "$TMUX_PANE" '#{@cockpit_name}'` is not `Datasec/MPS-R268` (control `-t %0` prints another name); `tmux list-panes -a -F '#{pane_id} #{@cockpit_name}'` shows exactly one line with that name and its id equals `$TMUX_PANE`; `pwd -P` is not the project dir.
