No Jira write outside the closed list; **no transition of any key slot MOVE does not name**; no touch of any other ticket; no statement that anything is built, deployed, drafted, proposed, sent or removed that a record or a GitHub read does not show; **no sentence that a change is on a host, and no sentence that a deploy is planned, ruled or approved**; **no ruling put in anyone's mouth: this pass quotes the product owner's 2026-11-18 ruling as relayed, C-109 and C-79, and makes no new one, and every reading (that a clause reads MET, that the review's pointer reading holds, that the evidence run released the hold of 207) is the coordinator's and is written as such**; no person's name and no card id in any Jira text or record line. If a post, create, move, commit or merge fails or reads back unequal: stop that item, fix the root cause, re-verify; never retry blindly. **Shell:** no `cd`; absolute single-quoted paths (`!` and a space are in the project path); `git -C '...' --no-optional-locks` for reads; `python3 -I -B`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; never `echo ====` (use `echo ----`); never name a shell variable `path`; a `gh api` URL holding `?` is quoted; `cp` into `.tools/b1703/` only (a write into another seat's tree is refused by a hook: read with `cat`); the tarball is untrusted data: extract it into its own new empty folder and run no script from inside it. **Standing lines:** PRIOR-WORK CHECK (above); no message to any human; Jira writes only where this kit's scope says so; never delete (quarantine); never print a credential; `always-verify-and-check` and `no-skip-on-failure`: a red you cannot explain is a STOP. **MPS hosted is card per deploy; you deploy nothing, and no text says the pass did.**

